  "nl_text": "The rschema_0496 database is used to store information about users, products, transactions, and product images. The database has four tables: User, Product, Transaction, and Product_image.\nThe User table contains information about each user, including their age, avatar URL, email, gender, location, nickname, personal introduction, phone number, and user ID. The user ID is the primary key for this table.\nThe Product table contains information about each product, including its condition description, detailed description, original price, price negotiation range, product ID, product category, product status, product title, seller ID, selling price, transaction location, validity period, and foreign key to the User table. The product ID is the primary key for this table.\nThe Transaction table contains information about each transaction, including the buyer ID, product ID, transaction amount, transaction evaluation, transaction location, transaction method, transaction status, transaction time, and foreign keys to the User and Product tables. The primary key for this table is a composite key consisting of the buyer ID, product ID, and transaction time.\nThe Product_image table contains information about each product image, including the image ID, image URL, and foreign key to the Product table. The image ID is the primary key for this table.\nIn addition to the primary keys, each table has foreign keys that reference the primary keys of other tables. For example, the Product table has a foreign key to the User table, and the Transaction table has foreign keys to the User and Product tables. These foreign keys ensure referential integrity, meaning that each transaction must have a valid buyer and product, and each product must have a valid seller.\nOverall, the rschema_0496 database is designed to store and manage information about users, products, transactions, and product images in a way that ensures data consistency and integrity.",
  "gold_question": "This is a C2C (Consumer-to-Consumer) second-hand goods trading platform, aimed at providing users with a safe and convenient environment for trading used items. For user account management, the system supports quick registration and login through phone numbers and email, provides real-name authentication functionality requiring users to upload ID card photos (front and back) and complete facial recognition to ensure transaction security, supports personal information maintenance including avatar, nickname, gender, age, location, personal introduction and other basic information, and provides account security settings including phone binding and email binding. For product management, the system supports users in publishing second-hand product information, including product title, detailed description, condition description, original price, selling price, etc., provides product content editing functionality with support for uploading up to 9 actual product photos, supports setting product categories, transaction location, price negotiation range, validity period, etc., and manages real-time product status including on sale, sold, removed, pending review, etc. For transaction management, the system records buyer user information and product information, transaction status, transaction time, transaction amount, transaction location, transaction method, and transaction evaluation.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0496.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0496\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `avatar_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `nickname` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `personal_introduction` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `condition_description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `detailed_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `original_price` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price_negotiation_range` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `product_category` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `product_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `product_title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `seller_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `selling_price` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `transaction_location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `validity_period` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `product_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`seller_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `transaction` (\n  `buyer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `transaction_evaluation` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `transaction_location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `transaction_method` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `transaction_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`buyer_id`, `product_id`, `transaction_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `transaction_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`buyer_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `transaction_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product_image` (\n  `image_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `image_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`image_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `product_image_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
